From: kevinzhow <kevinzhow@local>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:00:53 +0800
Subject: Android camera source: no pipeline clock of its own,
 timestamps on arrival

The Android camera source (device.api rungic-android) timestamps frames with CLOCK_MONOTONIC. With it
providing the pipeline clock, camerabin lost sync when it added or removed the audio recorder; the
source now provides no clock and timestamps buffers on arrival.

Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-09-26
X-Rungic-Status: Inappropriate [the camera source is this project's Android camera bridge]
X-Rungic-Tests: none (gap: no scenario records video in Snapshot)
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/research/35
---
 aperture/src/camera.rs | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/aperture/src/camera.rs b/aperture/src/camera.rs
index fbe0f06..deca707 100644
--- a/aperture/src/camera.rs
+++ b/aperture/src/camera.rs
@@ -148,6 +148,14 @@ impl Camera {
     pub(crate) fn create_element(&self) -> Result<gst::Element, glib::BoolError> {
         let element = self.device().create_element(None)?;
         element.set_property("client-name", crate::APP_ID.get().unwrap());
+        if self.properties().get("device.api").and_then(|v| v.get::<String>().ok()).as_deref()
+            == Some("rungic-android")
+        {
+            // The Android source uses CLOCK_MONOTONIC. Keep camerabin on a
+            // stable system clock when it adds/removes the audio recorder.
+            element.set_property("provide-clock", false);
+            element.set_property("do-timestamp", true);
+        }
         Ok(element)
     }
 
